From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "adnan.drina" <adnan.drina@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:53:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(guardrails): loop escalation to a thinking profile

RHOAI3 E-1 (2026-10-02): a worker that repeats one identical call keeps
sending the same thinking-off request until the identical-call guard halts
it. When the stall guard emits its note for the THIRD consecutive identical
call, that worker's following model requests now use an escalation request
body from config; the escalation ends at the first edit (write_file, patch,
or a terminal sed -i / > src/ / tee src/), the first verification command
(run-verify.sh, advance.py), or after max_turns escalated requests (default
8). Then the normal body returns. A later third-call note may start a new
escalation. The guardrails are unchanged: the streak keeps counting and can
still halt; near-duplicate and refusal halts stay on the normal body.

Config: providers.<provider>.models.<model>.loop_escalation, falling back to
providers.<provider>.loop_escalation, {enabled, max_turns, request_body}.
request_body replaces the normal extra_body for escalated requests (chat
completions wire); its max_tokens is the output cap. Absent or disabled
config changes nothing. Reasoning from an escalated turn is echoed on later
turns through the existing model.reasoning_echo path (not bypassed).

agent.log lines carry the prefix [loop-escalation]: start (task, tool, args
digest), turn k/N, end reason=edit|verification|cap, and cap-hit when an
escalated response stops on finish_reason=length (logged before the
truncated response is discarded). State: agent._loop_escalation.snapshot().
Local extension.
